The assertion was changed from `Assert.Matches(ParseErrorMessage(), ...)` to a conjunction of two regexes. The old pattern matches `Refused to frame ... because an ancestor violates ...`, and the new pattern matches `Framing ... violates ...`. These are different browser messages, so one log line cannot match both, and `&&` makes this assertion always fail. The intent was clearly to accept either format, which needs `||`.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/ServerExecutionTests/WebSocketCompressionTests.cs" lines="104-117"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The test is meant to guard that framing is blocked with a CSP message. As written it fails on every browser version, including the one it is supposed to pass on, so it gives no signal either way.

